stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Queued : you send a command (admit)
    Queued --> Taken : current, mutant_a: worker takes the request (lock released)
    Taken --> Running : current, mutant_a: worker allocates and registers it
    Taken --> Disconnected : current, mutant_a: no free slot, or allocation fails
    Taken --> LostCancel : current, mutant_a: you cancel while it is taken (cancel returns false) [breaks CancelIsSeen]
    LostCancel --> Responded : the request runs to its end, ignoring your cancel
    Queued --> Running : design_a: worker takes and registers in one hold
    Queued --> Disconnected : design_a: no free slot, or allocation fails, in that same hold
    Queued --> Cancelled : you cancel while queued (cancel returns true)
    Running --> Cancelled : you cancel while running (flag set)
    Running --> Responded : the run ends before a cancel
    Responded --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]
    Disconnected --> [*]
    note right of LostCancel
        Shortest path (current, and mutant_a, which splits the hold again):
        Queued -> Taken -> LostCancel -> Responded
    end note
    %% Left out of this chart, as in the model:
    %%   - a request still queued at shutdown
    %%   - ordered-mutation tickets and spawn failure
    %%   - admit refused after shutdown (caller reports cancelled at once)
